 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532522,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You remodel your kitchen and decide to change out the tile floor. The floor measures 30 ft by 15 ft. One box of tile costs $45 and covers 10 ft<sup>2</sup>. How many boxes of tile should you buy, and what will it cost?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "45 boxes at a cost of $2,025.00"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The area of a rectangle is <span data-math=\"A = LW\"></span>where <i>L</i> represents the length and <i>W</i> represents the width.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = LW = \\left( {30{\\rm{\\ ft}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\rm{15\\ ft}}} \\right) = 450{\\rm{\\ f}}{{\\rm{t}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>Make conversion factors out of the equivalences of one box costing $45 and covering 10 square feet to answer the questions.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"450\\ {\\rm{ }}\\cancel{{{\\rm{f}}{{\\rm{t}}^2}}}\\left( {\\frac{{1\\ {\\rm{ box}}}}{{10\\ {\\rm{ }}\\cancel{{{\\rm{f}}{{\\rm{t}}^2}}}}}} \\right) = 45\\ {\\rm{ boxes}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"45\\ {\\rm{ }}\\cancel{{{\\rm{boxes}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{\\$ 45}}{{10\\ {\\rm{ }}\\cancel{{{\\rm{boxes}}}}}}} \\right) = \\$ 2,025\"></span></p>\n<p>You need 45 boxes of tiles. It will cost you $2,025.</p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
